# 4. APPROVED BUSINESS MODEL — NON-NEGOTIABLE

## Individual Student 5-Good

Student application
→ School preliminary review
→ One consolidated School forwarding list with one official decision attachment
→ One-time School-to-City forwarding
→ City shared review
→ Committee official decision.

## University of Da Nang

Eight configured member institutions:

- DUT
- DUE
- UED
- UFL
- UTE
- VKU
- VNUK
- SMP

They share ONE School Review Unit:

`unit-udn`

The original Student institution must remain distinct.

There is one shared School reviewer account under the approved current configuration.

UDN sends ONE consolidated list with ONE common decision document per award season.

Do not expose administrative controls that unintentionally divide UDN forwarding into eight separate batches.

## City

Authorized reviewers use one shared City review workspace.

No mandatory Officer assignment.

No separate staff workload allocation subsystem.

No active ResolutionCase workflow.

## Committee

Authorized Committee accounts review actual recorded results and execute official decisions.

No fictional meetings, hearings, voting or questioning system.

## Collective

Collective Student 5-Good uses TT01–TT04.

Collective applications go directly to City.

No in-system School preliminary forwarding for Collective applications.

## AI

AI remains optional and non-intrusive.

AI does not execute official judgments, assignments, forwarding or Committee decisions.

UX-S4 must preserve all of these constraints.

