# 16. PRODUCTION CORRECTNESS

Admin mutations can affect many Student applications.

Prioritize correctness.

Verify:

- Canonical validation.
- Server-side permission checks.
- Database uniqueness where applicable.
- Version/concurrency controls.
- Safe failure behavior.
- Auditability.
- Historical data preservation.
- No unauthorized bulk mutation.
- No silent cross-season effects.

Examples:

Changing an institution mapping must not silently reassign historical submitted applications.

Changing criteria must not silently re-evaluate official human judgments.

Changing a user role must not automatically create unauthorized Committee authority.

Closing a season must not ignore existing confirmed forwarding or decision states.

Do not mark a mutation successful until the backend confirms it.

